# Never commit real secrets. config.js IS tracked on purpose: it only holds
# public values (site URL, phone, and the Supabase anon key, which is safe to
# publish because Row Level Security enforces access). If you ever add a
# service_role key or an SMTP password, put it in one of these instead:
.env
.env.*
secrets.json
